{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "version": "0.11.0",
  "candidateTag": "v0.11.0-prealpha.1",
  "summary": "This release uses stock OMP v18.18.0 as its engineering baseline. The 6 changelog entries below record the changes since v0.10.1. Historical receipts do not qualify these bytes.",
  "highlights": "- This release uses stock OMP v18.18.0 as its engineering baseline. The 6 changelog entries below record the changes since v0.10.1. Historical receipts do not qualify these bytes.\n- Show offline, tailnet, desktop, gateway, and reconnecting states without the amber warning color, which now means only that a session is waiting for you; access denial stays red.\n- Replace the mark with \"Portal\" across the app icons, public site, and artwork, and give Android notifications a monochrome status-bar badge instead of the full-color app icon.\n- Redesign **OMP Sessions** as the monochrome \"Signal\" system (ADR-049): color now marks only state (green live, amber your turn, red denied), the theme follows the system's light or dark scheme, text is self-hosted Geist, and the directory is one toolbar row, one elevated request card, plain rows, and floating trays with drawn icons.\n- Make the public site follow the system color scheme and serve the same self-hosted Geist files as the app; rendering the banner and social card no longer contacts Google Fonts.\n- Hide the in-session Hold action when the client acknowledges the last Ask section, even while directory metadata is delayed, and reject stale Hold actions for answered requests.\n- Restore the inset of the embedded request card on phones, where the client's compact composer padding had left the card's label against its top edge.",
  "combinations": "| role | combination |\n|---|---|\n| Linux host | Run 42755992436 succeeded (https://github.com/carrythroughsystems/omp-session-gateway/actions/runs/42755992436); OS/kernel versions and migration counts are not exported. |\n| macOS host | VirtualMac2,1, macOS 27.0 arm64; doctor 18/18, rollback 23/23; native addon 2145111837cbd80379249b7709bb482ad379620e6f438f30c8037b25137f8bc0. |\n| Windows host | Windows x86-64 build 26100; 4 CPUs, 8186 MiB; Administrator upgrade/rollback from v0.10.1 and fresh standard-account lifecycle; interactive logon, not unattended boot. |\n| Chrome and Chromium | Pixel 8 Pro, Android 17, Chrome 157.0.8103.46; BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: Galaxy S26 (16.0.0, chrome 152.0.7977.54) |\n| Safari and WebKit | TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPhone 17 Pro Max (26.6, safari 26.6.1); BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: iPad (10th generation) (27.0, safari 27.0) |\n| Android | Pixel 8 Pro, Android 17, Chrome 157.0.8103.46; BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: Galaxy S26 (16.0.0, chrome 152.0.7977.54) |\n| iPhone and iPad | TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPhone 17 Pro Max (26.6, safari 26.6.1); BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: iPad (10th generation) (27.0, safari 27.0) |",
  "stableRollback": "The selected predecessor is v0.10.1. Gateway rollback does not switch or restart the separately running OMP process. This release uses stock OMP v18.18.0. rollback --to selects only retained runtimes. Preserve configuration and readiness-token state; see docs/UPGRADE_ROLLBACK.md for predecessor compatibility and stopped-service recovery.",
  "changesToTest": "- Show offline, tailnet, desktop, gateway, and reconnecting states without the amber warning color, which now means only that a session is waiting for you; access denial stays red.\n- Replace the mark with \"Portal\" across the app icons, public site, and artwork, and give Android notifications a monochrome status-bar badge instead of the full-color app icon.\n- Redesign **OMP Sessions** as the monochrome \"Signal\" system (ADR-049): color now marks only state (green live, amber your turn, red denied), the theme follows the system's light or dark scheme, text is self-hosted Geist, and the directory is one toolbar row, one elevated request card, plain rows, and floating trays with drawn icons.\n- Make the public site follow the system color scheme and serve the same self-hosted Geist files as the app; rendering the banner and social card no longer contacts Google Fonts.\n- Hide the in-session Hold action when the client acknowledges the last Ask section, even while directory metadata is delayed, and reject stale Hold actions for answered requests.\n- Restore the inset of the embedded request card on phones, where the client's compact composer padding had left the card's label against its top edge.\n- Qualify stock OMP v18.18.0 on every host lane. Requalify all thirteen lanes, including session-lifecycle and Push-triage scenarios, on these exact signed bytes; historical receipts and canaries do not transfer.",
  "plannedBoundary": "- Planned qualification: Debian 13 x86-64; macOS 27.0 (26A428) arm64 in a Virtualization.framework guest (VirtualMac2,1, ADR-033); a disposable Windows Server 2025 host (the Administrator lifecycle and a fresh standard-user install); Chrome on the physical Pixel 10 Pro, including its background-Push lane; and real iPhone, iPad, and Galaxy devices in TestingBot's cloud. Every lane must pass against these exact signed bytes before stable promotion; the plan is not evidence.",
  "candidateRollback": "The selected predecessor is v0.10.1; pruning keeps it installed as the recorded rollback target. Gateway rollback does not switch or restart OMP. Historical fork-era recovery is documented separately in docs/UPGRADE_ROLLBACK.md.",
  "qualification": {
